{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/284968-dark-ages-fae-help","id":284968,"title":"Dark Ages Fae Help","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-10-17T08:16:33-07:00","id":284968,"title":"Dark Ages Fae Help","content":"After all these years I've finally got round to thinking about writing a Dark Ages Fae adventure for an online Con. I'm reading properly through the book for the first time and am particularly interested in the Glastonbury Compact. Are there any sourebooks, adventures or unofficial fan stuff related to this that I could read for inspiration? Thanks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4114-steerpike65","name":"steerpike65","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-17T05:23:33-08:00","id":314400,"title":"","content":"Official: no.<br /> <br /> Unofficial: The Shattering hadn't happened yet. You could say that True Fae/Fae-blooded Welsh went along with the mortal Welsh to the south of what would become the US. I think that really depends on how you want to portray the True Fae. It would mean that it's the first European fae presence there, as House Eiluned wouldn't be hooking up with the Kachinas for about three hundred years yet. Try reading Isle of the Mighty if you'd like some inspiration for how to portray Europe after the compact, or even fae leaving the UK at that point in history. Hope this helped.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3920-sarah-rps","name":"Sarah RPs","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"38"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-24T10:56:17-08:00","id":320894,"title":"","content":"There IS some stuff about it \u2013 admittedly oblique kind of stuff \u2013 that can be found in the <b>Vampire: the Dark Ages</b> book <i>House of Tremere</i> in the appendix about Meerilinda's chantry, not far from Glastonbury Tor. It offers and interesting look into what came in the aftermath of the unlikely alliance's removal of the 'night demons' that infested the area. There is also even MORE oblique mention about it in the <i>Dark Ages: Tremere</i> novel... I want to say that there's another book too, but I am at work right now and unable to dig into the question.<br /> <br /> <b>Edit:</b> Oh, it's in <b>Dark Ages: Mage</b>, as suggested on the bottom of page 171 of <b>Dark Ages: Fae</b>!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>B.I.G. Bird spreads the word: Anybody with a heart votes love<br /> <a href=\"https://absintheandthorns.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">https://absintheandthorns.obsidianportal.com/</a></i>","edited":{"userid":409,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/409-phaolan","user":"Phaolan","date":". 11-24-2014, 05:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/409-phaolan","name":"Phaolan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar409_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"478"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}